	"knownBoundaryRisks": [
		"scripts/sync-devcontainer.sh excludes every scripts/* path except itself and the scripts/worktree/* runtime, which the isolated-worktree cutover added explicitly alongside its template-owned ownership rule. Any further template-owned script under scripts/ still requires the same paired cutover — an is_excluded include plus an ownershipRules entry ahead of scripts/template/** — or its declared syncPolicy merge is a lie.",
		"The sync script can advance .template-ref despite unresolved conflicts or review-only outcomes.",
		"The sync script --dry-run still mutates Git remotes and fetch state.",
		"init-new-project.sh validates neither repository identity nor all generated paths before destructive writes.",
		".devcontainer/devcontainer.json#initializeCommand is an object of named host entries and only the capture-warp-env entry is capability-gated (claude_warp). The prepare-container-env entry is core: it must never be gated, renamed, or folded into a gated sibling, because runArgs names the --env-file it writes — a render that drops it produces a devcontainer whose docker run fails at create."
	]
}
